                <pb facs="0760" n="675" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg675"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/2591: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Jefferson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-06-05T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 5, 1919, 5
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your April 28, 2 [<hi rendition="#italic">3</hi>] p.m.</p>
                <p>If American merchants are to be expelled, Department wishes to be kept closely
                    informed in ample time to take any action which might appear desirable. Has
                    expulsion decree been repealed?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
